title: The Missing Planet
subtitle: Our investigators have found Kamino, and what it is hiding.
tags: event
view-if: kamino_hunt >= 3 and not kamino_known
max-visits: 1
priority: 4
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_clones.svg
on-arrival: kamino_known = 1; kamino_early = 1; evidence += 2; jedi_suspicion += 1.5
achievement: kamino_early

= The Missing Planet

The missing world is **Kamino**, a planet of endless ocean and of cloners. The Kaminoans greet our envoys as expected guests. Their client, a Jedi Master named Sifo-Dyas, ordered an army of clone soldiers for the Republic ten years ago, they explain. It is nearly ready: hundreds of thousands of troopers, cloned from a bounty hunter named Jango Fett, with millions more to come.

No one in the Senate authorised it. No one in the Jedi Order admits to knowing. Somebody has been paying for it all this time.

- @oversight: Bring it before the Senate and place the army under Senate oversight.
- @decommission: Demand that the army be decommissioned.
- @secret: Keep it secret and keep investigating.

@oversight
subtitle: A secret army, made answerable to the Senate. Needs a majority.
on-arrival: {!
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.65, guild: 0.4, rim: 0.55, sec: 0.5, ind: 0.6, pal: 0.3, cis: 0.4}, true);
Q.ko_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Kamino Oversight Act', Q.ko_vote);
if (Q.ko_vote >= 50) { Q.army_oversight = 1; Q.evidence_public += 1; Q.fear += 3; if (Math.random() < 0.4) Q.chips_found = 1; this.achieve('oversight'); }
else { Q.fear += 4; Q.evidence_public += 0.5; }
Q.grand_plan -= 4;
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if army_oversight : The Senate takes formal custody of the clone army, which will stay on Kamino under a Senate committee's supervision. [? if chips_found : Our inspectors find something the Kaminoans did not want found: an organic chip in every clone's brain. ?] Somewhere, a Sith Lord's careful plan has just become much harder. ?][? if not army_oversight : The revelation causes uproar, but no majority agrees what to do. The army stays on Kamino, in limbo, answerable in practice to whoever pays the Kaminoans. ?]

@decommission
subtitle: Removes the army entirely. The Republic would face any future war without it.
on-arrival: {!
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.45, guild: 0.55, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.1, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.2, cis: 0.6}, true);
Q.kd_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, '-army');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Kamino Decommissioning Act', Q.kd_vote);
if (Q.kd_vote >= 50) { Q.kamino_army = 0; Q.sec_relation -= 10; Q.hawk_dissent += 10; Q.grand_plan -= 8; this.achieve('no_army'); }
Q.evidence_public += 1; Q.fear += 3;
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if not kamino_army : The Senate orders the army disbanded. The Kaminoans are paid off and the clones are given new lives as settlers on a dozen frontier worlds. If war comes, the Republic will have to fight it some other way. ?][? if kamino_army : The Senate refuses to throw away "the Republic's only army". It stays on Kamino, waiting. ?]

@secret
subtitle: +1.5 evidence and a chance to learn more; the risk is that whoever paid for it notices.
on-arrival: {! Q.evidence += 1.5; Q.grand_plan -= 2; if (Math.random() < 0.3) Q.chips_found = 1; if (Math.random() < 0.3) Q.leak_pending = 1; !}

The Caucus says nothing publicly. Our agents trace the payments: through the Banking Clan, through Damask Holdings, and into accounts controlled by someone in the Chancellery's orbit. [? if chips_found : One Kaminoan technician, bribed, admits that every clone carries a "behavioural modification chip". ?]
